@* Brain UI: the Brain's screens on the Devbook pane (local ADR 0040).

   Every Backlog.* import is written as @@using global::Backlog.Something, for
   the reason Capture.UI's imports give: this project's root namespace is
   Backlog.Modules.Brain.UI, the Razor generator emits these directives inside
   that namespace without a global:: prefix, and a bare "Backlog" binds to
   Backlog.Modules.

   No Devbook pane namespace is named here: the components that render on
   Devbook's viewer import it in their own file, so the one declared edge stays
   visible where it is taken. *@
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Brain.Abstractions
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Devbook.Abstractions
@using global::Backlog.SharedKernel
@using global::Backlog.SharedKernel.Markdown
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Buttons
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Devbook
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Feedback
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Icons
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Inputs
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Layout
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Markdown
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Overlays
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection
